{
  "id": "16-restored-in-christ",
  "title": "Restored in Christ",
  "tenet": "Receive mercy and pray with hope",
  "durationMs": 83760,
  "audioAsset": "kingdom/16-restored-in-christ.mp3",
  "transcriptAsset": "assets/kingdom/16-restored-in-christ.json",
  "text": "What if your first step after a fall were toward Christ, rather than deeper into shame?\n\nA woman once kept a cracked cup at the back of her cupboard. Whenever she saw it, she remembered the day she had broken it and hidden the pieces. At last she brought it into the light and told the truth. Her father did not ask her to pretend it was whole. He sat with her, helped her clear the sharp fragments, and gave her a sound cup to carry. Truth opened the way to repair. Hiding had only left her afraid to reach into the cupboard.\n\nChristian faith takes the spiritual struggle seriously, yet Scripture does not say that each lapse gives demons authority over you. The accuser speaks condemnation; Christ calls us to confess and receive mercy. John's first letter says the blood of Jesus cleanses us from sin, and Paul says there is no condemnation for those in Christ. Come promptly to God, tell the truth, make repair where needed, and take the next wise step. Christ is the new Adam. We are being renewed in his likeness; we do not earn back Eden by flawless effort. Jesus gave his disciples authority to serve, and told them to rejoice above all that they belong to God. Pray for healing, freedom, and even changed patterns of thought. Prayer is a privilege, not a guarantee of a particular outcome or a substitute for care. Ask the Holy Spirit to grow love, courage, and service in you today.",
